WEBVTT

00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:04.450
Welcome back. Let's start with a question.

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:08.710
How often do you feel like you're simply reacting

00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:12.800
to change rather than truly leading through it?

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:19.800
This brings us to a critical focus area, leading yourself through change.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.260
This isn't just about managing shifting timelines.

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:27.060
It's about intentionally managing your own inner state,

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:32.800
your energy, your focus and stability so you can become the anchor your team needs.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:37.280
In the Athleadership framework, your wellbeing is not a luxury.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.620
It's a competitive advantage that

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:43.100
fuels your resilience and agility under pressure.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:46.800
It's the foundation of sustainable high performance.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:50.840
I'll give you an example from my own life. A few years back,

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:54.670
I was trying to do it all. You know what that looks like.

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:55.950
Running a business,

00:00:55.950 --> 00:01:00.800
caring for my family and ending up physically and emotionally exhausted.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:04.660
But my team really felt that. My family felt it.

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:07.800
I wasn't leading. I was just surviving.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:14.230
It was only when I made my own wellbeing a non-negotiable and protected my

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:19.800
time and recovery that I was able to lead effectively through changes again.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:24.230
Now it's your turn. In your playbook, you'll find a drill for this.

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:28.800
Your action is to define what you want to get out of this experience.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:33.760
By identifying one specific pressure point you're feeling right now

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:38.800
and one wellbeing practice you can implement this week to manage it.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:43.270
And here's your challenge. Look at your calendar for the next week.

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:46.800
Does your schedule reflect what you say is important?

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:50.410
If not, what's one small change you can make to

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:53.800
better align your time with your intentions?

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:54.780
And remember,

00:01:54.780 --> 00:02:00.160
part of that alignment is protecting the time for your own development.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:04.620
Make sure you block time on your calendar for this journey.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:07.800
It's a non-negotiable. Invest in yourself.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:12.830
Once you've done that, I'll see you in the next video where we'll explore

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:17.800
how this focus on self-leadership turns into a multiplier for your team.
